{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And there was no bread, etc., for the famine was heavy, etc.</b> The meaning is: because of the heaviness of the famine, they would eat an astonishing amount and consume all the bread. And indeed our own eyes have seen — may our souls be spared — in the two years of famine that were in the West [Morocco], that a single person would eat the ration of ten people and still be hungry in his stomach — may the Compassionate One shield us."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 47, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:49:25.871861786Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}